                <pb facs="0291" n="287" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg287"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1163AM33/60: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-03-05T15:00:00-05:00">March 5, 1938—3 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>78. Shanghai’s 284, February 19, 5 p.m. Department suggests that, if you have not
                    already done so, you ask the Foreign Office to give serious attention to the
                    substance of Shanghai’s telegram under reference, as further illustrative of the
                    general situation referred to in Department’s 33, February 2, 5 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
